.TH smi-format "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-format \- Format the source files of a project recursively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-format
.IR PATH ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-format
finds, under every
.IR PATH ,
recursively, the source and configuration files a Java, Python, Clojure or Common Lisp project
contains, formats them in place, and prints the path of each formatted file on its own line.
A
.I PATH
is usually the project directory; a single file is formatted too when its name is in the list
below.
.PP
The formatter is the command line formatter of IntelliJ IDEA,
.IR /opt/idea/bin/format.sh ,
which the
.B idea
package installs. The file list, the directories left out and the output stay the same if the
formatter is replaced, so a script or a habit that uses
.B smi-format
does not depend on it.
.PP
The code style is that of the IDEA project the file belongs to, from its
.I .idea
directory, and the IDEA defaults for a file outside any IDEA project.
All the found files are given to one run of the formatter, which takes some
seconds to start.
.SH FILES FORMATTED
.TP
Java and the JVM
.IR *.java ,
.IR *.kt ,
.IR *.kts ,
.IR *.groovy ,
.IR *.gradle ,
.IR Jenkinsfile ,
.IR *.properties ,
.IR *.xml ,
.I *.xsd
.TP
Python
.IR *.py ,
.IR *.pyi ,
.I *.pyw
.TP
Clojure
.IR *.clj ,
.IR *.cljs ,
.IR *.cljc ,
.IR *.cljd ,
.IR *.edn ,
.I *.bb
.TP
Common Lisp
.IR *.lisp ,
.IR *.lsp ,
.IR *.cl ,
.I *.asd
.TP
Common to all
.IR *.json ,
.IR *.yaml ,
.IR *.yml ,
.IR *.toml ,
.IR *.md ,
.IR *.sql ,
.IR *.sh ,
.IR *.html ,
.IR *.htm ,
.IR *.css ,
.I *.js
.PP
Left out are minified
.I *.min.js
and
.I *.min.css
files and
.IR package-lock.json ,
which are generated.
.SH DIRECTORIES LEFT OUT
.PP
Version control, IDE, build output, dependency and cache directories, wherever they are under
.IR PATH ,
because what they hold is not source, or is not the project's own:
.IR .git ,
.IR .hg ,
.IR .svn ,
.IR .idea ,
.IR .vscode ,
.IR target ,
.IR build ,
.IR out ,
.IR dist ,
.IR .gradle ,
.IR .mvn ,
.IR node_modules ,
.IR .venv ,
.IR venv ,
.IR __pycache__ ,
.IR *.egg-info ,
.IR .eggs ,
.IR .tox ,
.IR .mypy_cache ,
.IR .pytest_cache ,
.IR .ruff_cache ,
.IR .ipynb_checkpoints ,
.IR .cpcache ,
.IR .shadow-cljs ,
.IR .clj-kondo ,
.IR .lsp ,
.I .calva
and
.IR .cache .
.SH OUTPUT
.PP
Standard output lists the absolute path of each formatted file, one per line, as the formatter
reaches it. A file already in style is listed too, as the formatter reports it the same way.
A file the formatter has no support for is not listed: IntelliJ IDEA formats Python only with the
Python plugin, Clojure only with a Clojure plugin such as Cursive, and has no Common Lisp
formatter, so with a bare installation those files are found but left as they are.
Messages of the formatter, other than its banner and counts, go to standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_IDEA_HOME
The IntelliJ IDEA installation,
.I /opt/idea
by default.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every found file was given to the formatter, and it succeeded. Also when nothing was found.
.TP
.B 1
No
.IR PATH ,
a
.I PATH
that does not exist, or no formatter installed.
.TP
.B other
The status of the formatter.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Format a project and see what was formatted:
.RS
.nf
smi-format ~/sources/my-project
.fi
.RE
.PP
Format two modules and count the files:
.RS
.nf
smi-format api client | wc -l
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
.PP
The files are changed in place. Commit, or otherwise keep, the work before the first run, so the
changes of the formatter can be reviewed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-install-package (1)
.SH AUTHOR
setmy.info
